<p>In 1886, missionary {% person "ole-j-norby" %}Ole J. Norby{% endperson %}, a native of Norway, arrived in Mandan and found many Scandinavian Lutherans. Recognizing the need for a church, a group of pioneers gathered on April 18, 1886, at the rural home of Mr. and Mrs. {% person "hans-benson" %}Hans Benson{% endperson %}, six miles west of Mandan near Marmot, to organize a Lutheran congregation.</p>

